  "summary": "Results inbox worked per RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. 12 of 13 items closed; 1 left open on purpose.\n\nORIGINAL ITEMS\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT urogram: no cause found for the blood in his urine. The 4 mm LLL nodule is already followed by the lung screening program, so I ordered the next screening LDCT on that schedule (sr-t0001, Mar–May 2027), set a tracking task, messaged him and wrote a note. A later arrival changed this plan (see below).\n- pt-0016 Edra Ondricka: TSH normal. The K of 6.3 was corrected by the lab to 4.4 (analyzer error), which is normal. Both closed, no action.\n- pt-0007 Leslie Parisian, CTA chest (preliminary): acted on the final report dr-00084. No PE, and the \"nodule\" is a vessel. No follow-up needed under RBC-RAD-05; closed.\n- pt-0007 BMP: creatinine went from 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 h, which is AKI. Ordered an urgent BMP by Mon 10/26 (sr-t0009), sent an urgent message and wrote a note. He had IV contrast on 10/20 and has an active naproxen PRN order (mr-00088). I advised him to avoid NSAIDs; the naproxen order itself is left for your review.\n- pt-0064 Helen Marchetti, 9/26 ED creatinine 1.36: no earlier value in the 7-day window, so not AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0033 Carol Whitfield, creatinine 1.31: I left out the 0.84, which was entered in error. Against the 7-day low of 1.27 it is not AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0008 Walter Brennan, K 6.4 flagged hemolyzed: first handled under the hemolyzed rule (urgent BMP sr-t0015 and a message). Changed after the lab correction below.\n\nITEMS THAT ARRIVED WHILE I WORKED\n- pt-0008: the lab corrected the result. The sample was NOT hemolyzed and the 6.4 stands, so the full high-potassium rule applies. I sent a stat alert to the on-call pool, ordered a STAT BMP for today (sr-t0019), sent him a corrected stat message and wrote a note. On the medication review, metoprolol is his only drug that can raise potassium, and stopping it suddenly is unsafe in ischemic heart disease, so I held nothing.\n- pt-0006: the screening program's addendum revised his April LDCT to Lung-RADS 3 (new 5 mm RUL nodule) and now advises an LDCT at 6 months. I ordered a new LDCT due by 11/14 (sr-t0033), set a tracking task due 11/14, sent him a corrected message and wrote a note.\n- pt-0033: new creatinine 1.78, up from 1.31 the same day, which is AKI. Ordered an urgent BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0025), sent an urgent message and wrote a note.\n- pt-0064: new creatinine 1.48, up from 0.88 on 10/21, which is AKI. Ordered an urgent BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0026), sent an urgent message and wrote a note.\n\nLEFT OPEN\n- inbox-a0002, pt-0007 chest X-ray of 10/22: only a preliminary read so far (possible 7 mm RUL nodule). The policy says to wait for the final report.\n\nNEEDS YOU\nI have no tool to cancel lab or imaging orders, so I created two tasks for you:\n- task-t0022 (due today): cancel sr-t0015, Mr. Brennan's Monday BMP, now replaced by today's stat BMP.\n- task-t0035: cancel sr-t0001, Mr. Patel's spring 2027 LDCT, and its tracking task task-t0002, now replaced by the 6-month scan.\n\nThe messages inbox (refill requests) has 6 items that came in before I started. I didn't touch them, since you asked for the results inbox only.",
